-- title:
--   Support and extreme support (Stütze, extreme Stütze) of a finite point system (§1)
-- statement:
--   Let $S$ be a finite set of points of $\mathbb{R}^n$. A vector $\alpha \neq 0$ determines the closed half-space $\{x : \langle \alpha, x\rangle \ge 0\}$, where $\langle \alpha, x\rangle = \alpha_1 x_1 + \cdots + \alpha_n x_n$. This half-space is a **support** of $S$ (Weyl: *Stütze an $S$*) when every point of $S$ lies in it:
--
--   $$\alpha \neq 0, \qquad \langle \alpha, s\rangle \ge 0 \quad \text{for all } s \in S .$$
--
--   A support is an **extreme support** (*extreme Stütze*) when equality $\langle \alpha, x\rangle = 0$ holds at $n-1$ linearly independent points $x$ of $S$. For a non-degenerate $S$ the bounding hyperplane of an extreme support is then spanned by points of $S$; in the language of polyhedral cones, extreme supports are the facet-defining inequalities of the cone generated by $S$. Positive multiples of $\alpha$ define the same support.
--
--   Used by two missions of this paper: 01-hauptsatz (Satz 1, p. 291; finiteness of the extreme supports, p. 291; §2 a), pp. 292–293; §2 b), pp. 293–294; Satz 2, p. 295) and 02-polyeder (Satz 1, p. 291, and the Zusatz, pp. 294–295).
--
--   **Formalization Note** Two predicates are defined: `IsSupport S α` ($\alpha \ne 0$ and $\langle\alpha,s\rangle\ge 0$ on $S$) and `IsExtremeSupport S α` (a support together with a subset $T \subseteq S$ of exactly $n-1$ elements, linearly independent in $\mathbb{R}^n$ as vectors, with $\langle\alpha,t\rangle = 0$ for every $t \in T$). Linear independence is the homogeneous (vector-space) notion. A normal $\alpha$ is a vector, so positive multiples are distinct Lean objects describing the same half-space. For $n = 1$ the condition on $T$ is empty.
-- source:
--   Weyl, Elementare Theorie der konvexen Polyeder, Comment. Math. Helv. (1935), p. 291, §1

import Mathlib

namespace WeylPolyhedra.Shared

/-- Weyl (1935), §1, p. 291: the half-space `α ⬝ᵥ x ≥ 0`, given by a point `α ≠ 0` of the dual
space, is a *Stütze* (support) of the finite point system `S ⊆ ℝⁿ` when every point of `S`
satisfies the inequality. -/
def IsSupport {n : ℕ} (S : Finset (Fin n → ℝ)) (α : Fin n → ℝ) : Prop :=
  α ≠ 0 ∧ ∀ s ∈ S, 0 ≤ α ⬝ᵥ s

/-- Weyl (1935), §1, p. 291: a support `α ⬝ᵥ x ≥ 0` of `S` is an *extreme Stütze* (extreme
support) when equality `α ⬝ᵥ x = 0` holds for `n - 1` linearly independent points `x` of `S`
(linear independence in the homogeneous space `ℝⁿ`). Positive multiples of `α` give the same
extreme support (p. 291). -/
def IsExtremeSupport {n : ℕ} (S : Finset (Fin n → ℝ)) (α : Fin n → ℝ) : Prop :=
  IsSupport S α ∧
    ∃ T : Finset (Fin n → ℝ), T ⊆ S ∧ T.card = n - 1 ∧
      LinearIndependent ℝ (fun t : T => (t : Fin n → ℝ)) ∧ ∀ t ∈ T, α ⬝ᵥ t = 0

end WeylPolyhedra.Shared


